# Every dotenv file is secret unless it is explicitly an example.
#
# This was a per-file denylist (.env.deploy, .env.local, .env.*.local), so a new one
# was untracked-but-not-ignored — and `git add -A` swept .env.analytics, holding a live
# Cloudflare API token, straight into a commit. GitHub's push protection caught it;
# nothing reached the remote. A denylist only protects the files someone remembered.
.env
.env.*
!.env.*.example

# Local Vite overrides (e.g. VITE_API_BASE) and editor/preview launch config
.env.local
.env.*.local
.claude/launch.json
